  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Michael King delivered six innings of one-run baseball. The bullpen unraveled when it mattered most.",
    "what_this_means": "They never led. Merrill tied it in the seventh with a home run, but that was the floor. Not a springboard. The Braves scored six runs in the eighth while Peralta and V\u00e1squez combined to record one out. A five-run rally in the ninth came too late. Ten strikeouts from the lineup and nine left on base: this is inconsistency in its clearest form. King gave them a chance to win. The offense and bullpen made sure they didn't.",
